=== NOTES ===

1. AtomicsObserver / vehicleIntID flow:
   ADR-004 #11 (phase-42a amendment) introduces the AtomicsObserver
   pattern, but the per-Atomic vehicleIntID is still NOT threaded
   through router.Routable / router.Writer. The snapshotWriter
   sidesteps this by resolving vehicle_id BIGINT inside the INSERT
   via the vehicles.vin UNIQUE index. If a future prompt extends
   router.Writer to take vehicleIntID directly, the helper can drop
   the SELECT v.id subquery without changing its public surface.

2. Per-destination wrappers (0012-0018):
   This helper is consumed by 7 wrappers — climate_snapshot,
   motor_snapshot, tire_pressure_snapshot, media_snapshot,
   safety_snapshot, location_snapshot, security_event. Each
   wrapper supplies (table, columnFor) and a thin
   `func New<Dest>Writer(db *pgxpool.Pool) (router.Writer, error)`
   constructor. The wrapper is also the right home for any
   destination-specific value coercion (e.g. ftproto enum ->
   string, int32 -> int64) before delegating to snapshotWriter.

3. Compound type rejection:
   The helper deliberately does not handle compound atomics
   (Location lat/lng pairs, Doors flags, TireLocation per-corner
   values). codec.Atomic always carries flattened atomics post-
   codec.Decode (codec_test.go:TestDecode_AtomicValuesAreFlat
   enforces this), so the per-destination wrappers should never
   send a compound atomic to snapshotWriter. If they do, the
   "unsupported value type" error path catches it.

4. PowerShell-7 quirks reused:
   - Resolve-Path on the log file is unnecessary here because the
     log lives at the repo root's .github tree, not under web/;
     no Push-Location is performed.
   - .github/prompts/ is gitignored (.gitignore:83-89 + repo memory)
     so `git add -f` is required to stage the log artifact. The
     commit step uses `git add -f` for the log only.
   - go test runs natively under pwsh -File without needing
     .\node_modules\.bin\... shenanigans (those quirks are
     web-build-specific).

